{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T15:38:14.702Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"624c62caf26f4f7373cf910f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-slack-standup-kovw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Cursor-complete standup reporting windows: build from a certified event boundary and retain the exact next boundary"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Build a standup from a certified event boundary and retain the exact next boundary so crashes or late/backdated appends do not silently skip work between time windows. Overlap check (re-run 2026-10-27): pm history events / listMutationEvents supply cursor-resumable mutation facts; pm-observer (evidence budgets), pm-context (context-pack cursor), pm-slack (outbox resume cursors) use cursors for their own domains; this package's --since/--days/--compare date windows and snapshots select periodic views. No sibling or CLI command builds standup reporting from a retained event boundary, so this adapts the core mutation cursors to standup reporting without adding another event journal. Acceptance: (1) restart after rendering produces the same packet; (2) a late append appears once in a later admitted window; (3) missing history/cursor coverage marks the report incomplete rather than empty."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-27T15:38:14.702Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T15:38:14.702Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","v